  "body": "### Summary\nAs a maintainer building the app in Xcode, I want a build with no compiler warnings, so that a new warning (often a concurrency bug) is seen instead of lost among old ones.\n\n### Report\nOperator, Xcode device build of `dev-swift` `45b25dff` (2026-11-11): 5 warnings, from 3 distinct sites:\n1. `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/SmallStores/NotificationLedger/NotificationLedgerStore.swift:37` and `:50`, \"Result of call to 'update' is unused\". The private `update(_:_:)` (`:94`) returns a `Bool`, and `recordNews` and `markCheckedIfDue` ignore it. This warning shows up twice, once in the app build and once in the HFRStorage build.\n2. `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/ForumScopeBar.swift`, \"Converting non-Sendable function value to '@isolated(any) @Sendable (TopicSource) -> Void' may introduce data races\". The cause is the `let select: (TopicSource) -> Void` at `:9` (added by #744).\n\n### Scope\n- Fix each site at its cause rather than silencing it:\n  - (1) Either mark the private `update` `@discardableResult`, or write `_ =`, depending on whether the Bool means anything to those two callers.\n  - (2) Give the closure the isolation it actually runs with, likely `@MainActor`.\n- Check whether CI shows these warnings. If it does not, say why, and propose (do not apply) a CI step that fails on new warnings.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] An Xcode build of the app and of HFRKit shows 0 warnings at these sites.\n- [ ] No behaviour change; existing tests green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
